WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.080
A page from a playscript.

2
00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.320
Speech after speech runs edge to edge.

3
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.640
That's prose.

4
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.710
Then a woman hides in a garden bower.

5
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.550
She is left alone, and
suddenly her lines break short.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.720
It begins: "What fire is in mine ears?

7
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.260
Can this be true?"

8
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.710
Same character, new shape.

9
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.740
So why does Beatrice
suddenly switch to rhyme?

10
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:27.690
In this mission, you'll learn to tell
verse from prose just by the look of the

11
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.740
page.

12
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.900
You'll collect the tools
of wit: puns, opposites,

13
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:35.330
and quick replies that
twist a rival's own word.

14
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.620
And you'll test a theory: is verse
just for the people at the top?

15
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.420
Your mission: explain why
Beatrice switches to rhyme.
